Well, after being a total winner at all ??Hack ???'s, I
figured that Nethack 3.0 would be a slight challenge.  Boy was I wrong!!
It is NAS-TEE, but you can live if you are patient...

Mild spoilers...







It seems best to go down levels SLOOWLY, like in Moria. Take your time
going down the dungeon.  You'll find enough food to survive.  Also, unlike
in previous versions, pets are EXTREMELY useful and can SAVE YOUR BUTT.
Train everything you can and find those magic whistles...

My best game was a Samurai that found boots of speed - he died when he ran
out of food and was surrounded by demons on level 16.  If you go down
slowly, you'll eventually find good armor.  Another spoiler:  find an
altar to your god and dump armor and weapons on it BEFORE using them -
they'll be uncursed and you'll be able to take them off if they are bad.
I like the new game, since it now seems to be as challenging as Original
Rogue with lots more role-playing possibilities.  I only wish I could actually
*use* credit cards :-)

